The same unaddressed modal change also orphans the manual-download prompt (`mod-acquire`), which has worse consequences than a lost form.

Besides `Event::CloseModal`, `apply_linked_result` (`Event::LinkedResult`, sent by `finish_linked` and by `InstallMod` when another linked operation completes) sets `modal` to `""` or `"mod-result"` without checking which dialog is open.

When either arrives while a `mod-acquire` prompt is shown:

- the prompt disappears, but its backend wait (`await_manual_acquisition` in `crates/gui/src/backend.rs`) keeps watching the folders;
- for `ChangeModVersion`/`UpdateMod` and `RestoreModFile` the prompt was the only way to cancel that wait;
- for linked server creation `allow_cancel` is false, so the creation stays pending and its creation key stays held;
- a prompt queued in `acquisition_prompts` behind the replaced one is shown only when `ModAcquisitionEnded` arrives for the replaced id (`end_mod_acquisition`), which happens only if the user somehow supplies the file, so the queued operation also waits with no prompt.

Expected, in addition to the above: a completion from another operation never closes or replaces a `mod-acquire` prompt (or, if it must, puts it back afterwards), and queued prompts are shown as soon as the on-screen prompt is no longer visible.

Locations at `0c4051d677cc427a3dbcba98528f345373625989`: `crates/gui/src/controller.rs` `Event::CloseModal` (7302), `apply_mod_acquisition` / `end_mod_acquisition` (8370-8430), `apply_linked_result` (8616).

