**Crate:** `ephervex-gui`

**Commit:** `beee756`

## Behavior

Slint 1.17.1's `ComboBox` ignores writes to `current-value` from outside (slint-ui/slint#11970). The visible selection keeps following `model[current-index]`, and Slint logs `ComboBox: \`current-value\` writes don't change the selection. Use \`current-index\` instead.`

Several combos in `crates/gui/ui/app.slint` are driven only through `current-value`:

- create instance: Minecraft release, loader, loader version (`current-value <=> root.create-minecraft` and siblings);
- create server: Minecraft release, loader, loader version;
- Change Loader dialog (`current-value <=> root.loader-change-selected`);
- mod results per page (`current-value: root.mod-page-size-label`);
- Minecraft preview release (`current-value: root.minecraft-preview-release`);
- artifact cache custom unit (`current-value <=> root.artifact-cache-custom-unit`).

## Actual behavior

When Rust sets the backing property to a value other than `model[current-index]` (a suggested or default release, a restored preference), the dropdown shows one entry while the dialog submits another.

## Expected behavior

The displayed entry and the submitted value always agree. Drive the selection through `current-index` (look up the index of the wanted value) and cover that the displayed text matches the submitted value.
